      "description": "A strict row subset of the full index, in the same schema and the same sort, so a hit found here resolves its geometry exactly as a hit found there: same feature_id, same geometry_ref, same name_norm. A row is included when it is (a) a primary row at level 0, 1, 2, 3 -- country, dependency, region, county, localadmin; or (b) an alternative-name row at level 0; or (c) a level-4 locality row, primary or alternative, whose Overture cartography.prominence is >= 50. prominence is Overture's own 1-100 cartographic ranking, populated on every locality and on nothing else; it is guidance rather than a measurement, so this is a recall boundary and not a claim that an excluded place is unimportant.",
